{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/867324-the-original-sin-unwilling-diablerist-character-brainstorming","id":867324,"title":"The Original Sin - Unwilling Diablerist Character Brainstorming","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-17T20:26:21-07:00","id":867324,"title":"The Original Sin - Unwilling Diablerist Character Brainstorming","content":"So, in order to not spam the Ask The Question thread, I'll move it into it's own thread.<br /> I want to discuss, ask for help, critic, and so on about a very specific and atypical character concept. Here is the basic idea:<br /> <br /> 1. Long, long time ago, in a Requiem far away, there was a Serial Diablerist. Serial Diablerist cooked up a very diabolic scheme; scheme of attaining Godly Power By Diablerizing A Lot Of People. In order to *get* a lot of people to diablerize, Serial Diablerist kidnapped and embraced relatively safe targets in the mortal world, then, well, diablerized them.<br /> <br /> 2. One of the victims is the main character. Probably a very normal type of girl. Your classical protagonist who is probably a little sad and depressed, and lonely (which makes her a good target for our SB).<br /> <br /> 3. Diablerie goes wrong for reason X. Serial Diablerist ends up being Diablerized instead of our Protagonist. <br /> <br /> 4. Kindred community decides against killing the Protagonist, but isn't very welcoming either.<br /> <br /> That's the basic setup. There is a lot of things that can be specified and might provide interesting hooks. <br /> <br /> - Identity and history of the Serial Diablerist. Obviously, it will be a pretty central character. Who were they? What was their motvation? <br /> - Why Diablerie ended up being reversed? Was this done on purpose, and SB is secretly wants to come back overtaking Protagonists body, after she becomes accepted by the local community? Was it just luck? Final effort of SDs victims? Intervention of a Strix? <br /> - How local community is going to react to this? Why they let Protagonist live? Is Ordo Dracul interested in her? Maybe, if SD was a Dragon, they act like she is SDs successor? Maybe some of their colleagues act like she is just an extesion, or even worse, a temporary change that will be over soon? <br /> - What important factors would shape gameplay experience of such character? What consequences should be expected?<br /> <br /> I love playing characters with heavy psychological problems. I think this is a fantastic opportunity for personal horror. Protagonist definitely would consider her Humanity important, and I definitely enjoy idea of playing someone who is basically a neonate in terms of experience while wielding powers of a much older vampire. Obviously, this character would work best in a game with higher starting BP and some XP.<br /> Even without that, though, I can see using the &quot;diablerie makes you powerful&quot; as a very nice tool for explaining why character is raising in power so quickly (player characters tends to do that); accelerated growth could be framed as blossoming fruits of that original diablerie; after all, it wasn't very normal amaranth, so why not? I think it provides a lot of fun drama potential.<br /> I also think that - if I understand correctly - Blood Sympathy of Protagonsit would be very, very fucked up, if she inherited all of SDs Sympathies, including ones SD got through previous diableries.<br /> What kind of tropes, character builds, hooks, personality ideas, building blocks of a character in general would you suggest for playing her? What kind of fiction do you find inspiring for this kind of challenge? Do you think it would work better in a solo game, or would it shine placed in contrast to more &quot;normal&quot; characters? Do you think that letting such character live is too much of a fiat? What kind of reactions in other Vampires this character might provoke? What kind of interesting Persistent and Personal Conditions do you think would be fitting to equip this character with? What kind of merits - both straight-from-the-book and homebrew - do you think could emphasize the dark and forbidden and unwanted power? <br /> <br /> For disciplines, I'm torn. I like image of using Ride the Wave to be physically powerful and hating it; but I also love idea of character who really wants to remain Human, and who tries to tap into Beast's power as little as possible, being blessed with Domination; I think that character who is really good at it, but has moral and ethical problems with using it pragmatically could be a blast to play. Especially if deck is stacked against her, and Domination is her only ace in the sleeve, only real advantage she can use to win. <br /> <br /> Sorry for bad structure and incoherent thoughts; bad case of insomnia + being bored = low quality posting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T04:51:58-07:00","id":867489,"title":"","content":"A few thoughts. <br /> 1) Amaranth is a Humanity 1 breaking point, which means you're rolling a chance die to avoid degeneration every time. Some method of avoiding draugr-hood should be considered here for the first guy, and likely we're starting at Humanity 6 for your main character, which means we're talking about suffering the clan bane from the start. Given that, you need to give serious consideration to what clan we're talking about here, since that's going to have an immediate effect. Normally, there's a bit of a transition period here. You've lost that, and its going to have an immediate &quot;Not Human!&quot; effect on her psyche.<br /> <br /> 2) You can't accidentily diablarize someone. Even revenants in the midst of a hunger frenzy won't diablerize someone. Diablerie is always a choice. You can choose to Ride the Wave with goal of committing Amaranth, you can be Dominated into consuming someone's soul, a strix can do it while possessing your body, but its not something that happens by mistake. Diablerie is an innately <i>wrong</i> act. Making it into something that can be slipped into kinda cheapens the entire thing and undermines what we know of diablarie. That means there's another, third player involved in this mess.<br /> <br /> 3) Your protagonist is now a wack job. She's hearing voices in her head to drive her nutty, telling her to go kill more people and eat more souls. She's addicted to diablerie now. Every Kindred knows this, and will look at her as a ticking time bomb. At minimum, we're talking about a schizophrenic addict until the Tainted Condition goes away, and likely some traces of it after that as well. Also, remember that she's not just addicted to diablerie, but vitae as well. Can't diablerieze without sampling the vampire blood.<br /> <br /> 4) Diablerie doesn't create new blood sympathies.<br /> <br /> 5) There's a few Theban/Cruac rituals on top of Auspex 3 and Mehket dreams that can divine the truth of the matter. If we're talking about this being a mystery, you'll have to take these powers into account. <br /> <br /> Personally, I would not forgive a diablerist without putting them under the control of a very powerful elder who would watch the neonate like a hawk. Likely a member of the Ordo Dracul, who not only are better at staying awake during the day, but likely are interested in the character as a study. And likely put under some powerful Dominate commands or the Vinculum. Likely, going to have difficulty finding a cotorie outside of those assigned to watch over her, given the lack of trust. Who wants to be friends with an addict that might kill you for their next rush?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T07:15:15-07:00","id":867542,"title":"","content":"An option: The Serial Diablerist has been found out. For some reason leaving the city is not an option. Instead, they attempt to take over another body - the PC's. Either through mistake or design, the victim remains in control, but is it permanent? She now has to beware of an enemy within and their contingency plans outside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T07:37:49-07:00","id":867552,"title":"","content":"Check out the En bloodline. They are the poster-children for Serial Diablerist kindred. They have a dark passenger (parasite) that trades its favors (Gifts of the Alu) to the host, and pushes them to commit Amaranth. Eventually, if the host degenerates to a Draugr, the parasite is able to inhabit the body as a full vampire and often goes on a ridiculous tear of destruction and mayhem,.<br /> <br /> Imagine this scenario - The En antagonist is rampaging the city, and has already killed and devoured one or two high ranking Kindred. A blood hunt is called, the troops are rallied, but the war isn't going well for the Domain. The PC in question is about to be the latest victim, but something happens and the victimization backfires, the PC turns the tables somehow, and the En is devoured instead.<br /> <br /> Thematic Questions/Conflicts/Themes:<ul><li>One faction of Kindred hail the PC as a hero, and look the other way at the veins that are riddled across their soul, it was self-defense afterall. Another group appreciates the service and will erect a monument in honor of their sacrifice, but Diablerie is Diablerie, and can never be condoned.</li> <li>Did the parasite transfer? Is the PC now an En as well? How do they handle this new creature / spirit / manifestation of the beast as it whispers to and tempts them? Who do they confide in?</li> <li>Is there a shadow cult in the city? Was the reverse-diablerie actually an accident? Is the PC truly a hero, or were they deliberate bait? Who's pulling the strings?</li> <li>Memories of the previous victims are now in the PCs head. There are secrets buried there, and someone needs them desperately. Another Kindred sees the spark of their childe/sire/lover in the PC and needs that relationship in their unlife still.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}